1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,554
Part two. The last money out the door.

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:04,702
Look at who wrote the biggest checks.

3
00:00:04,748 --> 00:00:07,651
Nvidia. Microsoft. Google.

4
00:00:07,906 --> 00:00:11,006
AMD. TSMC. Broadcom.

5
00:00:11,122 --> 00:00:11,947
Micron.

6
00:00:12,365 --> 00:00:15,952
Together, about $26 billion into the IPO.

7
00:00:16,707 --> 00:00:17,461
Notice something?

8
00:00:17,879 --> 00:00:19,807
These are Anthropic's suppliers.

9
00:00:19,876 --> 00:00:21,096
In Zitron's view,

10
00:00:21,258 --> 00:00:22,524
they were topping up a customer,

11
00:00:22,547 --> 00:00:23,882
so it can keep paying them,

12
00:00:24,114 --> 00:00:26,309
and so early investors could cash out.

13
00:00:26,982 --> 00:00:28,665
That's the last money out the door.

14
00:00:29,025 --> 00:00:30,569
Retail buyers near the top,

15
00:00:30,604 --> 00:00:33,182
he notes, lost money almost immediately.

16
00:00:33,855 --> 00:00:36,073
Here's why that matters for everyone else.

17
00:00:36,166 --> 00:00:38,290
Next in line is OpenAI.

18
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:40,276
It just raised $11 billion,

19
00:00:40,589 --> 00:00:44,281
at a $1.25 trillion valuation.

20
00:00:44,769 --> 00:00:47,044
Reports say it wanted $30 billion,

21
00:00:47,404 --> 00:00:49,320
at $1.4 trillion.

22
00:00:50,098 --> 00:00:52,861
Oddly, one Bloomberg report stressed the money had

23
00:00:52,896 --> 00:00:54,498
actually been wired and received.

24
00:00:54,927 --> 00:00:56,390
Zitron had never seen that.

25
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,178
And OpenAI's numbers,

26
00:00:58,259 --> 00:00:59,328
as he cites them,

27
00:00:59,362 --> 00:01:02,834
are rough. A loss of $10.9 billion in

28
00:01:02,927 --> 00:01:06,282
one quarter, on about $10 billion of revenue.

29
00:01:06,851 --> 00:01:08,395
Yes, margins improved:

30
00:01:08,662 --> 00:01:12,633
from about minus 150% to minus 100%.

31
00:01:13,202 --> 00:01:16,151
And its newest model got a cold reception,

32
00:01:16,418 --> 00:01:17,927
even from its cheerleaders.

33
00:01:18,357 --> 00:01:20,876
He expects OpenAI to need more money early

34
00:01:20,946 --> 00:01:21,608
next year.

35
00:01:22,177 --> 00:01:23,581
But its biggest backers,

36
00:01:23,616 --> 00:01:25,764
he says, chipped in only a few hundred

37
00:01:25,799 --> 00:01:28,481
million, because they're short on cash too.

38
00:01:29,258 --> 00:01:30,837
So his question is blunt.

39
00:01:31,267 --> 00:01:33,949
After Anthropic soaked up this much money,

40
00:01:34,111 --> 00:01:36,073
who's left to fund OpenAI?

41
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:38,593
And the biggest supplier of all just went

42
00:01:38,674 --> 00:01:40,543
quiet on something important.
